":"cod-gr","role":"present"}],"source_ids":[21,22]},{"controller_id":"cod-pnc","sovereign_id":"cod","status":"dominant","confidence":"medium","basis":"default_state_presence","as_of":"2026-10-01","zone":"Rural villages of Bolenge secteur (Wendji, Bongonde, Ikengo, Libinza, etc.) and Mbandaka secteur (Bamanya, Ilelenge, Lolifa, Boyeka, Monzambi Ibonga)","evidence":"No reports of armed-group activity in Mbandaka territory's rural secteurs; state presence via police posts and secteur administration, with customary chiefs settling local disputes.","unit":"CD4101-mbandaka","run_id":"drc-swarm-1","presence":[{"entity_id":"customary","role":"present"}],"source_ids":[21]}],"sources":{"21":{"url":"https://www.mediacongo.net/article-actualite-163519_mbandaka_un_civil_blesse_lors_d_echanges_de_tirs_entre_la_garde_republicaine_et_la_police.html","title":"Mbandaka : un civil blessé lors d'échanges de tirs entre la Garde républicaine et la police","publisher":"Mediacongo","date":"2026-05-09"},"22":{"url":"https://fr.allafrica.com/stories/202511270307.html","title":"Congo-Kinshasa: Procès en flagrance contre un policier accusé de meurtre à Mbandaka","publisher":"AllAfrica","date":"2025-11-27"}},"units":{"CD4101-mbandaka":"Mbandaka, capital of Equateur province, is far from the eastern conflict zones and has no armed group holding territory. Day-to-day order in the city's communes (Mbandaka, Wangata) and neighbourhoods is kept by the Congolese National Police (PNC, including GMI/LENI units), with FARDC (Bokala military camp) and Republican Guard elements garrisoned in the city. Reported incidents in 2025-2026 are police abuses (extortion of moto-taxi drivers, a killing at the central market in Nov 2025) and a May 2026 firefight between Republican Guard and police elements, not challenges to state control. Rural villages of the Bolenge and Mbandaka/Wangata secteurs along the Congo and Ruki rivers have no reported armed-group activity and are assessed as default state (PNC) presence."}}